  "title": "Lantern Convoy",
  "rules": [
    "All three explorers are controlled. Movement follows public walls; co-location and crossing are allowed. Each explorer carries at most one cargo and one lantern.",
    "Cargo pickup/drop and delivery use exact cells. Cargo can be passed to an adjacent free carrier; lantern and charge can be passed to an adjacent non-holder.",
    "Switch-on light consumes one battery per tick, including the toggle tick. The last paid unit still illuminates its snapshot; no charge regenerates.",
    "A hazard is directly sensed within distance one, or within distance four while lit by a lantern at distance at most three. Walls do not occlude this discrete glow.",
    "Hazards pulse on the native clock. Armed contact damages carried cargo; destroyed cargo disappears from active cargo and never delivers.",
    "Relay copies the freshest available sample to adjacent peers in one hop. Sample time is retained; stale armed values are never shown as current hazard state.",
    "Public cargo telemetry excludes private priorities. Unseen hazard sprites are hidden in role views; complete state is debug-only."
  ],
